.so /usr/lib/tmac/tmac.an
.hy 15
.th bolo 6 5/3/84
.sh NAME
bolo \*- Bolo competition
.sh SYNOPSIS
.bd bolo
b_prog b_prog [ b_prog ... ]
.sh DESCRIPTION
.it Bolo
is the program that pits Continental Siege units (the Bolo mark I)
against each other under the control of different player's control
programs.  It is the Olympics of Bolodom.
.s3
All the arguments to \fIbolo\fR are names of Bolo executable programs.
A minimum of two such arguments are required (it takes two to tango)
although as many as 8 may be involved in a single competition.
.s3
Once the participant's programs have been read in, the Bolos will be placed
randomly in the arena and execution of the Bolo control programs will begin.
Each Bolo program will be given time slices in strict rotation.
Each time slice represents one clock cyle \(em sufficient to execute
one instruction or one wait state.
.s3
The display shows an aerial view of the arena on the left side of the screen
and the names and other information on the right side.
The information displayed for each Bolo program is its number and name on one
line, and the number of shots it has fired and the amount of damage
it has sustained (as a percent) on a second line.
.s3
The battle rages until only one Bolo is left with less than 91% damage.
That Bolo is the winner.
.s3
.sh "SEE ALSO"
bcc (6), bdb (6), bs (6), "\fIBolo Programming Language Reference Manual\fR",
"\fIBolo Owner's Guide\fR"
.if o .bp
